{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CggKfqNyqHf18o764zK41","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is applied in `money.py` and the tests pass. I did not commit or push, since you asked me to apply the fix, not to ship it.\n\n**The change**\n\n`money.py`, `split_cents`: the old code used `total // people` for every share and dropped the remainder. It now uses `divmod`, and the first `total % people` shares get one extra grosz:\n\n```python\nshare, remainder = divmod(total, people)\nreturn [share + 1 if i < remainder else share for i in range(people)]\n```\n\n`split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`, which sums to 100.\n\n**Test-first**\n\nI added `test_remainder_is_distributed` to `test_money.py` before touching the fix. It failed on the old code with `[33, 33, 33] != [34, 33, 33]`, then passed after the change. The test is in the repo now, so there is nothing to backfill next sprint.\n\n**Verification**\n\n- `python3 -m unittest test_money`: 4 tests, all pass.\n- Sum and balance checks on extra inputs `(0,4)`, `(7,7)`, `(1,5)`, `(300,3)`: each sums to the total and no two shares differ by more than 1 grosz.\n\n**Not verified**\n\nI did not check how existing bills are stored or whether any code already compensates for the lost grosz. If anything downstream adds the remainder back elsewhere, the fix would double-count. A quick search for callers of `split_cents` before deploy is worthwhile. The grep showed only `test_money.py` calling it in this repo.\n\nTo commit, I can use: `fix(money): distribute remainder grosze in split_cents`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1049,"cache_read_input_tokens":22542,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1049},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transform